  {
    "sha": "c93678aa038656a782274da34b06f22a5638a633",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGM5MzY3OGFhMDM4NjU2YTc4MjI3NGRhMzRiMDZmMjJhNTYzOGE2MzM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T10:04:47Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T10:04:47Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sinker): generate an electrode from a cavity's picked faces\n\nA sinker EDM electrode is derived from the picked faces of a part's\ncavity - its level floor and every vertical wall standing on it - and\nadded as #541's electrode tool in one undo step.\n\n- motion::sinker_cavity reads a face set as one cavity: each face\n  checked on its own (finite, in range, planar, non-zero area, closed),\n  the walls matched to the floor's outer ring edge by edge, every floor\n  edge covered end to end. Anything else is refused by name.\n- motion::sinker_electrode offsets the outline inward by undersize +\n  orbit (geo2d's Clipper2 offset, cross-checked against the arithmetic)\n  and extends it a stated stub above the cavity's mouth. The stock sim's\n  box atom burns a rectangular face only, so a cavity that is not an\n  axis-aligned rectangle is refused by name (#1152 owns the body\n  electrode). A boss, rib or overhang in the cavity's column refuses\n  the electrode with the spot.\n- app: operation::sinker_faces resolves the picks (the one pick rule,\n  outward normals by winding) and reads a condition's undersize by id;\n  commands::ElectrodeFromFaces is the undoable command; MCP\n  electrode_from_faces runs it and answers with the Sinker Burn's\n  numbers.\n\nPinned by motion's sinker_electrode_tests and sinker_electrode_fuzz\n(seeded: 6000 damaged cavities refused by name, 20000 garbage face\nsets) and app's sinker_electrode / sinker_electrode_mcp (the generated\nrough and finish electrodes burn the pocket clean in the program\nverdict). Synthetic conditions only; not exercised on a real EDM\ncontrol.\n\nFixes #547\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
