  {
    "sha": "e1853f2224aea03f78aeaee36d7338bd98575e35",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGUxODUzZjIyMjRhZWEwM2Y3OGFlYWVlMzZkNzMzOGJkOTg1NzVlMzU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T03:31:07Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T03:31:07Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sinker): refuse unreadable part facets; warn a zero undersize\n\nReview of #1156 (NeoTech at dcaa3a36), over the refreshed #1136 and main:\n- electrode_from_faces refuses by name when the part's facets cannot be\n  read, instead of checking the cavity's column against an empty list.\n- The MCP reply gains a `warning` for a stated undersize of 0 (a\n  full-size electrode the size law will refuse as a rough or finish);\n  a condition never needs it (the machine file refuses a condition\n  undersized below its gap).\n- The orbit note names #544 as landed and #1355 for the size law.\n- Decision file: standing_in checks only the picked part; the rest is\n  the stock sim's and the fixture checks'.\n- Test fixture: SinkerBurnOp gains main's `orbit`.\n\nPinned by sinker_electrode_mcp::the_electrode_is_generated_and_burned_\nover_mcp_with_the_gui_commands (warning and note asserts).\n\nRefs #547\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
